    "equipment_fixture": "Six humans and four live AI, patrol arrival proved before moving guards away for isolated equipment damage comparison. Separate PVPVE runs cover AI combat.",
    "bullet_fixture": "Real input and server bullet traces. Crouched helmet target uses physical head body center; expected 16 HP remains unchanged. No assigned armor damage or trauma result.",
    "medical_interrupt_fixture": "SixLag01 fired after the three-second bandage completed. Prepare shooter aim before using bandage, preserve its actual active snapshot, fire immediately, and serialize the snapshot with the post-shot checks. Duration and consumption rules unchanged.",
    "ai_fixture": "Phase6A bullets bypass the old shield, so the old PVPVE driver allowed lethal bursts while serializing observation snapshots. Record the actual first hit and reacquisition in memory, end the burst through ordinary position/ammo fixtures, and serialize afterward. Isolate the separate real-bullet death/loot sample by approaching the guard from behind.",
    "inventory_fixture": "The old fixed 40 HP expectation after waiting three seconds ignored new bleeding. Verify real hit cancellation and unchanged medical count first, then ongoing bleeding without healing. Reset trauma only when arranging the next independent input-interruption baseline.",
    "combat_fixture": "The independent 20 HP lethal reload-interruption baseline clears trauma left by the preceding headshot sample, preventing an unrelated bleed tick from changing the required 20 HP bullet result.",
    "headshot_assertion": "When bleeding leaves less than 40 HP, a headshot health loss is capped by the observed remaining HP. Require actual Head bone classification in addition to the capped amount; a low-health body hit cannot satisfy a headshot assertion.",
    "visual": {
